Thus order: For each candidate, we need to allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness, assign operator (if needed), lock (if origin/destination), etc. For shift candidates we also need assign skill, assign compliance, load container, stage, verify, establish clearance, attach service window, validate route, finalize, allocate dispatch slot, execute dispatch.

For origin/destination: after confirm preparedness, assign operator, lock, then after leg assembled and loading authorized, we mark dispatch ready, allocate slot, execute dispatch.

Now we need to assemble leg and authorize loading before we can mark origin/destination dispatch ready and load containers for shift candidates.

